From 011a3fa97b256767d060d5623c217e6fc751b7f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Khanh Le <khanh.le.xr@renesas.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Feb 2026 22:37:16 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] arm64: dts: renesas: gray-hawk: rgid: Disable TMU to
 avoid early IRQ conflicts

On R-Car V4M board, after waking up from Low Power Mode (LPM), there is
interrupts conflict between application on Cortex-R and Linux kernel on
Cortex-A while the TMU driver is probing, leading to kernel panics in
early phase.

Disable TMU to avoid these conflicts.

Signed-off-by: Khanh Le <khanh.le.xr@renesas.com>
---
 .../dts/renesas/r8a779h0-gray-hawk-common-rgid.dtsi    | 10 +++++-----
 .../dts/renesas/r8a779h5-gray-hawk-common-rgid.dtsi    | 10 +++++-----
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/r8a779h0-gray-hawk-common-rgid.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/r8a779h0-gray-hawk-common-rgid.dtsi
index d7e8679f3373..c32b8e02fdd5 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/r8a779h0-gray-hawk-common-rgid.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/r8a779h0-gray-hawk-common-rgid.dtsi
@@ -946,23 +946,23 @@ &scif0 {
 };
 
 &tmu0 {
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &tmu1 {
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &tmu2 {
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
